{
 "encounter_id": "00772",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Hello doctor. I've got, um, my periods have gone irregular, and I'm getting hair on my chin and cheeks. I forget exactly when it began."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let's take it one at a time. How are your periods?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Every two or three months. Sometimes I skip. Before, they were regular."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "When did they change, roughly?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I think two years ago? Or maybe three. I really can't tell."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "That's fine. And the hair?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Dark, coarse hairs on the chin, and some on my upper lip. I wax it every week."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any acne, weight gain, or thinning on the scalp? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Some spots on my jaw. And I've put on about five kilos. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Are you on any medicine?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Metformin, 500 mg, twice a day, which my last doctor gave me, and spironolactone, 50 mg, once a day, for the hair."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Good. Any allergies to medicines?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Penicillin. As a child, I had hives. I haven't taken it since."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Thank you. Let me check your pulse and blood pressure. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Pulse 74, blood pressure 118 over 74, weight 68 kilos.",
   "pause": 12.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Is that normal? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Yes. The picture of irregular periods, excess hair and spots fits with something called polycystic ovary syndrome, but I'd like to confirm that with blood tests and a scan."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "PCOS? My cousin has it. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "It's very common. I'd like to arrange blood tests for hormones, including testosterone, and a pelvic ultrasound."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "The spironolactone can affect your periods and can harm a pregnancy, so are you using contraception? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Yes, condoms. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Keep doing that, please. I'd like you to continue the current tablets until we have the results. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Regular exercise and a balanced diet help a lot with this condition, even a small weight loss. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I'll try. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "If you miss a period and think you could be pregnant, take a test straight away and see me, because you must not take spironolactone in pregnancy."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I'll do that. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Or if the periods stop for more than six months, or you get heavy bleeding, come back to see me. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay. Thank you. ~"
  }
 ],
